course: dictionary
lesson: 12227
title: A conservatoire is a college for serious talent
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A conservatoire is a special college where people study music, singing, dance or drama to a very high level. Many people who go there want to become professional performers.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Maya practises the violin for three hours every day, because she hopes to study at a conservatoire.» Practising for hours and hoping to study suggest serious training, so a conservatoire must be a place for that kind of work.
explain: Some texts use the American spelling. «In America, the same kind of college is often called a conservatory.» The two words mean the same thing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Maya hopes to study at a college for very serious music training» still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: A conservatoire is a college where people study music, singing, dance or drama.
fact: People go to a conservatoire to train to a very high level, often for a career as a professional performer.
fact: The plural is conservatoires.
fact: In the US, the same kind of college is often spelled conservatory.
fact: The Royal Northern College of Music and the Paris Conservatoire are examples of conservatoires.
exercise: «Ella wants to study singing at a conservatoire when she is older.» What is a conservatoire? | A park with a stage for summer concerts | *A college for serious study of music, singing, dance or drama | A shop that sells musical instruments | A school for learning to swim
exercise: In the US, the same kind of college is often spelled as what? | conservator | conservative | conservation | *conservatory
exercise: Which of these would a conservatoire teach? | Car mechanics | Gardening | Cooking and baking | *Drama
test: «Jamal plays the cello so well that he hopes to go to a conservatoire.» What does a conservatoire teach? | Football and swimming | Maths and science only | *Music, singing, dance and drama to a very high level | Cooking and baking
test: What kind of training does a conservatoire offer? | Quick hobby lessons just for fun | Lessons only on weekends for beginners | *Serious training to a very high level | Lessons in how to build houses
exam: Which best explains a conservatoire to a friend? | A cafe with live music on Friday nights | *A college for serious study of music, singing, dance or drama | A kind of train that goes to the coast | A park with a stage for summer concerts
